<title>USA: A.O. Smith to acquire motor manufacturer.</title>
<headline>A.O. Smith to acquire motor manufacturer.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A.O. Smith Corp said Tuesday it reached a definitive agreement to acquire  UPPCO Inc, a privately held manufacturer of sub-fractional horsepower electric motors.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.  The company expects to complete the transaction within four weeks.</p>
<p>UPPCO, based in Monticello, Ind., has projected 1997 sales of about $80 million.  It is the world's largest manufacturer of sub-fractional horsepower &quot;C-frame&quot; motors.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
